# The Silent Monastery's bell tower (TSC_MonSpot_BellTower, Athletics).
# The rope did not rot.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_MonBellTower

== start ==
The ladder gives up its last rungs grudgingly, and the belfry is worse: eight hundred winters of pigeon ruin and rot-soft boards around a bell that is, itself, perfectly sound.

The rope is the thing. It did not rot away. It was cut - high, above the wheel, past any reach from below - and the coil hangs on a peg on the far side, tidy, deliberate, unreachable.

* [Think about who cuts a bell rope from above.] -> cut

== cut ==
Somebody climbed up here before the gate was barred and made certain of the house: that no brother, in whatever last hour, at whatever cost to his resolve, could weaken and ring for help that must not come.

The bell is fine. It has simply had nothing to say for eight hundred years, and nobody left it any means of changing its mind.

* [Climb down quietly.] -> end
